[K[34h[?25h[23d[3;1H Recorded incremental demo. Start from identified plain llama.cpp cf34d3113 (owned checkout,
 branch `demo-incremental-4`) and the frozen fast contract qwen36-quick-v1. Use
 engine.expert_streaming as your engineering method: read its guide and the current evidence, then
 make one meaningful behavioural change at a time. For every decision write the mechanism
 hypothesis and why the chosen component fits it in `hypothesis`, and in `uncertainty` name what
 is still unknown plus one alternative you are deferring and why. Candidates, not predetermined
 winners: demand fill first (expert_fill, with its source prerequisites installed but their
 switches off), then predictive reads (expert_pregate) only if the fill evidence supports
 continuing. For each intervention: integrate, build once through the builder (never rebuild
 unchanged source), run one cheap screen (a single lab run: output identity and engagement; its
 timing is preliminary), then if the screen passes run one 1-round ABBA against the current best
 under the same contract and keep or revert by the component's acceptance rule. Do not group
 unrelated active optimizations and do not tune parameters. After the last keep, run one 1-round
 ABBA of the plain baseline image versus the final image as the headline comparison, then finish
 with accept, reject or report_inconclusive and a short report of ms/token per arm, output
 identity and engagement.[23;103H[20;1H[30m[1m plain llama.cpp cf34d3113 · contract qwen36-quick-v1 · Jetson Orin Nano 8GB · Qwen3.6-35B-A3B[23;103H[m[1m CC activity · guidance the agent reads, capabilities it calls[24;103H[m[1;21r[1;103H[K
